<title>HONG KONG: Standard Chartered seen in HK$2 bln FRCD.</title>
<headline>Standard Chartered seen in HK$2 bln FRCD.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard Chartered Bank is planning to issue a HK$2 billion floating rate certificate of deposit issue, bankers said Friday.</p>
<p>The facility has a final maturity of five years with no put or call options.</p>
<p>Standard Chartered Investment Banking Division is the arranger. A co-arranger group is being formed.</p>
<p>An application will be made to the Hong Kong Monetary Authority to accept the issue as eligible for Liquidity Adjustment Facility, or discount window.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039</p>
</text>
